IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Fair Work Regulations 2009 (Cth) -- baseline-2026-11, shared helpers: the regulations' rounding rules and day
-- counting.
--
-- The only module in this encoding that imports daydate (the other modules import this one). Nothing here is a
-- question; the questions are in fwr-pay.l4, fwr-threshold.l4, fwr-fixed-term.l4 and fwr-claims.l4.
--
-- Edition: Fair Work Regulations 2009 (F2009L02356), Compilation No. 57, compilation date 1 October 2026 (register id
-- F2026C00996), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/F2009L02356.txt.

§ `Shared helpers`

-- Regs 2.13, 2.14: "Round the result to 3 decimal places. If the fourth decimal place is 5 or above, round it up."
-- Regs 3.02(5), 3.03(5), 3.07(5), 3A.03(5), 3A.05(5), 6.05(5), 6.07A(5): "rounded up or down to 3 decimal places,
-- rounding up if the result ends in 0.0005". Both are half-up rounding at the third place (all the amounts are
-- positive).
GIVEN `the result` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to 3 decimal places` MEANS (FLOOR ((`the result` TIMES 1000) PLUS 0.5)) DIVIDED BY 1000

-- Reg 2.13: "If the result is not a multiple of $100, round the result to the nearest multiple of $100. If the result
-- is a multiple of $50, round it up to the next multiple of $100."
GIVEN `the result` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest 100 dollars` MEANS (FLOOR ((`the result` DIVIDED BY 100) PLUS 0.5)) TIMES 100

-- The fee regulations, (3)(c): "round the result to the nearest multiple of 10 cents, rounding up if the result ends
-- in 5 cents."
GIVEN `the result` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest 10 cents` MEANS (FLOOR ((`the result` TIMES 10) PLUS 0.5)) DIVIDED BY 10

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- How many days the first day falls before the second (negative if after).
GIVEN `the earlier day` IS A DATE, `the later day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` MEANS Day `the later day` MINUS Day `the earlier day`

GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `falls on or before` IF Day `first` AT MOST Day `second`

GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `falls before` IF Day `first` LESS THAN Day `second`

-- "More than 3 months" after a day: later than the day 3 calendar months on (daydate's `add months`, which keeps the
-- day of the month and clamps a month end).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE, `number of months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `lasts more than` IF Day `the end` GREATER THAN Day (`add months` `the start` `number of months`)
